[[:db/retract 17592186122714 :answer-field/choices 17592186122715] [:db/retract 17592186122714 :answer-field/choices 17592186122716] [:db/retract 17592186122714 :answer-field/choices 17592186122717] [:db/retract 17592186122714 :answer-field/choices 17592186122718] [:db/retract 17592186122714 :answer-field/choices 17592186122719] {:db/id 17592186125019 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ \\\\ -3 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $A=PD{P}^{-1},$ find the second column of the matrix $P.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$, we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1.$\n\nSo, the second column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1.$ \n\nNow, we simply need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1.$ Computing $A-(-1)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 5\\end{aligned}]-(-1)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122714 :answer-field/correct "answer-fad88501-95d6-5d04-967e-1baa7d034ba2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfbfaed1-b369-5612-a2fa-36c8475ceb47" "answer-fad88501-95d6-5d04-967e-1baa7d034ba2" "answer-f9984cb1-95b5-56e2-9b37-0c405c4cefee" "answer-3641611f-7342-59e6-8eb1-e3d5c19f0c92" "answer-861930b1-88a9-5573-b1ac-9183d339e59f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfbfaed1-b369-5612-a2fa-36c8475ceb47" :answer/id #uuid "dfbfaed1-b369-5612-a2fa-36c8475ceb47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fad88501-95d6-5d04-967e-1baa7d034ba2" :answer/id #uuid "fad88501-95d6-5d04-967e-1baa7d034ba2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9984cb1-95b5-56e2-9b37-0c405c4cefee" :answer/id #uuid "f9984cb1-95b5-56e2-9b37-0c405c4cefee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3641611f-7342-59e6-8eb1-e3d5c19f0c92" :answer/id #uuid "3641611f-7342-59e6-8eb1-e3d5c19f0c92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-861930b1-88a9-5573-b1ac-9183d339e59f" :answer/id #uuid "861930b1-88a9-5573-b1ac-9183d339e59f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6f8bc57b-28dc-577c-84b2-316db148cde5" :activity/id #uuid "6f8bc57b-28dc-577c-84b2-316db148cde5" :activity/title "Diagonalizing a 2x2 Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049113 :activity/course 17592186046659 :